{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "> a(x: i8) = x + 127\n> b(x: i8) = (x-123)*(x-100)\n> c(x: i64) = -x\n> d(x: f32) = sqrt(x)\n> e(x: real) = sqrt(x)\n> g(x: u8) = 100 / x\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "ucas", "ucas": "a(x: i8) = x + 127\nb(x: i8) = (x-123)*(x-100)\nc(x: i64) = -x\nd(x: f32) = sqrt(x)\ne(x: real) = sqrt(x)\ng(x: u8) = 100 / x", "structured": false, "result": {"text": "> a(x: i8) = x + 127\n> b(x: i8) = (x-123)*(x-100)\n> c(x: i64) = -x\n> d(x: f32) = sqrt(x)\n> e(x: real) = sqrt(x)\n> g(x: u8) = 100 / x\n"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "> a(x: i8) = x + 127\n> b(x: i8) = (x-123)*(x-100)\n> c(x: i64) = -x\n> d(x: f32) = sqrt(x)\n> e(x: real) = sqrt(x)\n> g(x: u8) = 100 / x\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "wrap analysis of a:\n  x + 127   (i8)\n      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 127 points, e.g. x=-127\n      nsw fails: signed wrap at 127 points, e.g. x=1  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen\n  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 127 points, e.g. x=1\n      exact for: -128..0\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "wrap", "ucas": "wrap a", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "wrap", "exhaustive": true, "operations": [{"op": "x + 127", "type": "i8", "nuw": false, "unsigned_wrap_points": 127, "unsigned_wrap_example": "x=-127", "nsw": false, "signed_wrap_points": 127, "signed_wrap_example": "x=1", "c_ub": true}], "end_to_end": {"exact": false, "mismatch_points": 127, "mismatch_example": "x=1", "exact_for": [[-128, 0]]}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "wrap analysis of a:\n  x + 127   (i8)\n      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 127 points, e.g. x=-127\n      nsw fails: signed wrap at 127 points, e.g. x=1  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen\n  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 127 points, e.g. x=1\n      exact for: -128..0\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}, "isError": false}}
